<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arunachal Pradesh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arunachal Pradesh is the north-easternmost state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalayas</a>, bordering Bhutan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and Myanmar, with its capital at Itanagar. Home to many tribal peoples such as the Adi, Nyishi and Monpa, it was administered by the British as the North-East Frontier Tracts and after independence as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-east-frontier-agency">North-East Frontier Agency</a>. It became a state in 1987; China claims most of it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arunachal-pradesh.jpg" alt="Arunachal Pradesh" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arkadipta Chandra · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TawangMonastery-ArunachalPradesh-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
